<title>UK: Pearson rebounds from recent weakness.</title>
<headline>Pearson rebounds from recent weakness.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Pearson Plc rose on Friday in thin trade in what dealers said was a rebound from recent weakness, with some looking to restructuring moves when Marjorie Scardino takes over as chief executive in January.</p>
<p>Pearson gained 12p to 725p by 1104 GMT, having retreated this month from its record 782p set October 30.</p>
<p>&quot;We are seeing a technical bounce, that's all,&quot; said one dealer, &quot;although there is always the story about the company's potential break-up value.&quot;</p>
<p>--Andrew Langlands, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
